            <div xml:id="d867">

                <pb facs="1067" n="943" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg943"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.111/169</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wallace</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 29.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1295</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my cablegram No. 1232 of the
                    1st instant,<anchor n="35" xml:id="d867-f1"/> and to previous correspondence
                    regarding the situation of persons of dual nationality who come to France
                    without having discharged their military obligations under the French law, I
                    have the honor to transmit herewith in copy and translation a Note dated June
                    7th from the Ministry for Foreign Affairs, in which the status of the several
                    classes of such persons is defined.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh C. Wallace</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d867-a1.xml" xpointer="d867-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
